WEBVTT

00:04:35.197 --> 00:04:37.354
Storm's coming. And you boys?

00:04:37.355 --> 00:04:40.312
Your daddy? You are
smack in the middle of it.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:48.560
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:04:48.561 --> 00:04:50.067
Now, Dean! Go!

00:04:51.963 --> 00:04:53.907
He wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:04:53.908 --> 00:04:56.161
Saving people, hunting things...

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:57.880
The family business.

00:05:02.871 --> 00:05:05.625
Our whole lives have been
searching for this demon.

00:05:06.698 --> 00:05:08.509
Samuel Colt made a gun.

00:05:08.513 --> 00:05:10.698
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:05:11.557 --> 00:05:13.572
We finally know who
this demon's gonna be,

00:05:13.585 --> 00:05:15.545
And now, we know how to kill it.

00:05:16.079 --> 00:05:18.977
More and more demons
are walking among us.

00:05:25.561 --> 00:05:27.198
You're not my dad. Dean,
what the hell's going on?

00:05:27.213 --> 00:05:28.679
I think he's possessed.

00:05:30.134 --> 00:05:31.846
My plans for you, Sammy...

00:05:32.524 --> 00:05:35.248
You, and all the children like you.

00:05:40.852 --> 00:05:43.629
It's inside me. I can feel it. Shoot me!

00:05:43.633 --> 00:05:45.466
I can't hold on to it much longer!

00:05:49.902 --> 00:05:51.849
Why didn't you kill it?
We still got the colt.

00:05:51.853 --> 00:05:53.247
We still have the one bullet left.

00:06:32.341 --> 00:06:33.658
Get back

00:06:33.774 --> 00:06:36.087
Or I'll kill you. I swear to god.

00:06:36.104 --> 00:06:37.588
You won't.

00:06:37.592 --> 00:06:40.716
You're saving that
bullet for someone else.

00:06:43.735 --> 00:06:44.877
You want to bet?

00:07:07.231 --> 00:07:08.748
Oh, my god!

00:07:08.751 --> 00:07:10.079
Dad...

00:07:10.081 --> 00:07:12.629
Did I do this? Dad...

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:16.856
Dean...

00:07:31.123 --> 00:07:33.326
Significant passenger, space intrusion.

00:07:33.331 --> 00:07:36.276
Unresponsive. B.P. 180 over 50.

00:07:36.291 --> 00:07:39.697
B.P. 100 over 15. Heartbeat 95.

00:07:39.703 --> 00:07:42.317
Tell me if they're okay!
You have to stay still.

00:07:42.322 --> 00:07:43.617
Are they even alive!

00:08:10.473 --> 00:08:11.709
Sam?

00:08:18.983 --> 00:08:20.107
Dad?

00:08:22.084 --> 00:08:23.317
Anybody?!

00:08:29.953 --> 00:08:33.278
Shadow county, nurses' station.
How can I transfer your call?

00:08:34.224 --> 00:08:35.909
Of course.

00:08:35.913 --> 00:08:37.386
I transfer your call.

00:08:40.854 --> 00:08:42.778
Excuse me.

00:08:49.054 --> 00:08:50.628
Hi.

00:08:50.771 --> 00:08:54.299
I, uh... I think I was in
a car accident with my...

00:08:54.664 --> 00:08:56.937
Dad and my brother. I
just need to find them.

00:09:02.532 --> 00:09:03.346
Hello?

00:09:55.903 --> 00:09:56.919
Sammy...

00:09:58.222 --> 00:09:59.399
You look good...

00:10:00.083 --> 00:10:01.217
Considering...

00:10:10.274 --> 00:10:11.999
Man, tell me you can hear me.

00:10:15.812 --> 00:10:16.906
How's dad?

00:10:18.271 --> 00:10:19.386
Is he okay?

00:10:21.124 --> 00:10:22.638
Come on, you're the psychic.

00:10:23.332 --> 00:10:25.457
Give me some ghost
whispering or something.

00:10:26.423 --> 00:10:27.557
Your father's awake.

00:10:29.434 --> 00:10:30.836
You can go see him if you like.

00:10:31.403 --> 00:10:32.649
Oh, thank god.

00:10:35.075 --> 00:10:36.557
Doc, what about my brother?

00:10:37.024 --> 00:10:38.758
Well, he sustained serious injury.

00:10:38.763 --> 00:10:41.167
Blood loss, contusions
to his liver and kidney.

00:10:41.172 --> 00:10:43.077
But it's the head
trauma I'm worried about.

00:10:43.085 --> 00:10:45.297
There's early signs of cerebral edema.

00:10:45.302 --> 00:10:46.836
Well, what can we do?

00:10:46.852 --> 00:10:49.596
Well, we won't know his full
condition until he wakes up.

00:10:51.073 --> 00:10:52.068
If,

00:10:52.261 --> 00:10:53.609
He wakes up.

00:10:54.012 --> 00:10:55.008
If?

00:10:55.184 --> 00:10:57.157
I have to be honest. Screw
you, doc I'm waking up!

00:10:57.163 --> 00:10:59.669
Most people with his degree of injury
wouldn't have survived this long.

00:10:59.883 --> 00:11:01.429
He's fighting very hard.

00:11:01.761 --> 00:11:04.577
But you need to have
realistic expectations, son.

00:11:05.192 --> 00:11:06.609
Come on, Sam.

00:11:06.614 --> 00:11:09.386
Go find some hoodoo priest
to lay some mojo on me.

00:11:09.394 --> 00:11:10.588
I'll be fine.

00:11:13.443 --> 00:11:14.720
Sam?

00:11:16.922 --> 00:11:18.809
All right. Here.

00:11:19.521 --> 00:11:21.250
Give them my insurance.

00:11:23.061 --> 00:11:25.078
Elroy Mcgillicuddy?

00:11:25.852 --> 00:11:28.128
And his two loving sons.

00:11:30.484 --> 00:11:31.627
So...

00:11:33.101 --> 00:11:35.188
What else did the doctor say about Dean?

00:11:35.672 --> 00:11:37.038
N othing.

00:11:38.763 --> 00:11:39.726
Look...

00:11:39.982 --> 00:11:41.707
If the doctors won't do anything,

00:11:42.042 --> 00:11:43.717
Then we'll have to, that's all.

00:11:43.721 --> 00:11:45.450
I don't know. I'll find some...

00:11:46.224 --> 00:11:49.006
Hoodoo priest and lay some mojo on him.

00:11:50.583 --> 00:11:52.337
We'll  look for someone.

00:11:52.345 --> 00:11:53.679
Yeah.

00:11:53.845 --> 00:11:55.106
But, Sam...

00:11:56.331 --> 00:11:58.336
I don't know if we're gonna find anyone.

00:11:58.342 --> 00:11:59.416
Why not?

00:12:00.091 --> 00:12:01.829
I found that faith healer before.

00:12:02.075 --> 00:12:04.379
That was one in a million. So what?

00:12:04.381 --> 00:12:06.599
We just sit here with
our thumbs up our ass?

00:12:06.605 --> 00:12:07.977
No, I said we'd look.

00:12:09.561 --> 00:12:12.098
All right? I'll check under every stone.

00:12:16.714 --> 00:12:17.866
Where's the colt?

00:12:20.532 --> 00:12:21.887
Your son is dying,

00:12:21.893 --> 00:12:24.268
And you're worried about
the colt? We are hunting

00:12:24.272 --> 00:12:26.858
This demon, and maybe
it's hunting us too.

00:12:27.464 --> 00:12:29.826
That  gun may be our only card.

00:12:31.174 --> 00:12:32.568
It's in the trunk.

00:12:33.693 --> 00:12:35.916
They dragged the car
to a yard off of i-83.

00:12:35.924 --> 00:12:39.336
All right, you got to clean out that trunk
before some junk man sees what's inside.

00:12:39.342 --> 00:12:40.677
I already called Bobby.

00:12:40.844 --> 00:12:44.230
He's like an hour out. He's gonna
tow the Impala back to his place.

00:12:44.231 --> 00:12:45.519
All right. You,

00:12:45.713 --> 00:12:48.726
You go meet up with Bobby. You get
that colt and bring it back to me.

00:12:48.733 --> 00:12:50.969
And you watch out for hospital security.

00:12:50.983 --> 00:12:52.478
I think I got it covered.

00:12:58.514 --> 00:12:59.656
Hey.

00:13:01.913 --> 00:13:02.726
Here.

00:13:04.351 --> 00:13:05.669
I made a list of things I need

00:13:05.672 --> 00:13:07.568
That Bobby pick them up for me.

00:13:09.322 --> 00:13:10.266
Acacia?

00:13:11.352 --> 00:13:13.658
Oil of Abramelin? What's this stuff for?

00:13:13.664 --> 00:13:14.646
Protection.

00:13:19.492 --> 00:13:20.598
Hey, dad...

00:13:21.184 --> 00:13:22.598
You know the demon?

00:13:22.783 --> 00:13:26.036
He said he had plans for
me and children like me.

00:13:26.161 --> 00:13:28.127
You have any idea what he meant by that?

00:13:28.861 --> 00:13:30.717
No, I don't.

00:13:41.372 --> 00:13:43.847
Well, you sure know something.

00:13:47.322 --> 00:13:48.707
Oh, man.

00:13:49.052 --> 00:13:51.129
Dean is gonna be pissed.

00:13:56.703 --> 00:13:58.528
Look, Sam, this...

00:13:59.663 --> 00:14:01.656
This just ain't worth a tow.

00:14:06.442 --> 00:14:09.608
I say we empty the trunk,
and sell the rest for scrap.

00:14:12.153 --> 00:14:12.997
No.

00:14:15.557 --> 00:14:17.001
Dean would kill me if we did that.

00:14:18.485 --> 00:14:20.415
When he gets better, he's
gonna want to fix this.

00:14:21.679 --> 00:14:23.467
There's nothing to fix.

00:14:24.225 --> 00:14:26.788
The frame's a pretzel.
The engine's ruined.

00:14:27.531 --> 00:14:29.759
There's barely any
parts worth salvaging.

00:14:30.163 --> 00:14:31.158
Listen to me, Bobby.

00:14:32.371 --> 00:14:34.437
If there's only one
working part, that's enough.

00:14:35.443 --> 00:14:37.197
We're not just gonna give up on...

00:14:41.365 --> 00:14:42.568
Okay.

00:14:43.043 --> 00:14:44.250
You got it.

00:14:46.492 --> 00:14:47.797
Here...

00:14:47.982 --> 00:14:50.168
Dad asked if you could
get this stuff for him.

00:14:52.702 --> 00:14:54.236
What John want with this?

00:14:54.732 --> 00:14:56.466
Protection from the demon.

00:15:00.653 --> 00:15:01.639
What?

00:15:02.151 --> 00:15:04.840
Nothing. It's just... Bobby.

00:15:07.011 --> 00:15:08.427
What's going on?

00:15:24.904 --> 00:15:26.120
Come on, dad.

00:15:27.151 --> 00:15:28.538
You got to help me.

00:15:30.554 --> 00:15:32.867
I got to get better. I
got to get back in there.

00:15:38.751 --> 00:15:40.798
I mean, you haven't
called a soul for help.

00:15:41.533 --> 00:15:43.090
You haven't even tried.

00:15:43.573 --> 00:15:44.968
Aren't you gonna do anything?

00:15:45.764 --> 00:15:47.439
Aren't you gonna even say anything?!

00:15:51.293 --> 00:15:53.476
I've done everything
you have ever asked me.

00:15:54.252 --> 00:15:55.419
Everything.

00:15:55.584 --> 00:15:57.798
I've given everything I've ever had.

00:15:59.764 --> 00:16:02.249
Now you're just gonna sit
there? You're gonna watch me die?

00:16:04.732 --> 00:16:06.749
I mean, what the hell
kind of father are you?!

00:16:14.684 --> 00:16:16.028
What is that?

00:16:22.615 --> 00:16:24.057
I take it you didn't see that.

00:16:55.533 --> 00:16:56.538
Hey!

00:16:56.781 --> 00:16:58.419
I need some help in here!

00:17:00.831 --> 00:17:02.126
I can't...

00:17:02.362 --> 00:17:03.466
Breathe.

00:17:14.242 --> 00:17:16.487
Sammy, tell me you can
freaking hear me, man.

00:17:16.494 --> 00:17:17.679
There's something in the hospital.

00:17:17.683 --> 00:17:19.927
Now, you got to bring me back,
and we got to hunt this thing.

00:17:20.204 --> 00:17:21.269
Sam!

00:17:21.753 --> 00:17:22.889
You're quiet.

00:17:28.114 --> 00:17:29.757
You think I wouldn't find out?

00:17:29.764 --> 00:17:31.507
What are you talking about?
That stuff from Bobby.

00:17:31.511 --> 00:17:34.269
You don't use it to ward off a
demon. You use it to summon one.

00:17:34.565 --> 00:17:36.208
You're planning on bringing
the demon here, aren't you?

00:17:36.212 --> 00:17:38.487
Having some stupid macho showdown!

00:17:38.501 --> 00:17:41.438
I have a plan, Sam.
That's exactly my point!

00:17:41.444 --> 00:17:44.088
Dean is dying, and you have a plan!

00:17:44.295 --> 00:17:45.869
You know what?! You care more about

00:17:45.874 --> 00:17:48.329
Killing this demon than
you do saving your own son!

00:17:48.333 --> 00:17:50.319
No, no, no. Guys, don't do
this! Do not tell me how I feel!

00:17:50.324 --> 00:17:52.769
I am doing this for Dean. How?

00:17:53.092 --> 00:17:54.876
How is revenge gonna help him?

00:17:54.882 --> 00:17:56.898
You're not thinking about
anybody but yourself!

00:17:56.902 --> 00:17:59.237
It's the same selfish obsession!

00:17:59.271 --> 00:18:00.757
Come on, guys, don't
do this! That's funny,

00:18:00.793 --> 00:18:02.996
I thought this was your
obsession too. This demon

00:18:03.043 --> 00:18:04.469
Killed your mother,

00:18:04.473 --> 00:18:07.877
Killed your girlfriend. You
begged me to be part of this hunt!

00:18:07.884 --> 00:18:10.487
Now, if you killed that damn
thing when you had the chance,

00:18:10.494 --> 00:18:12.759
None of this would have happened.
It was possessing you, dad!

00:18:12.761 --> 00:18:13.918
I would have killed you, too! Yeah,

00:18:13.923 --> 00:18:15.710
And your brother would
be awake right now.

00:18:15.711 --> 00:18:17.438
Shut up, both of you! Go to hell.

00:18:17.653 --> 00:18:20.137
I should have never taken
you along in the first place.

00:18:20.143 --> 00:18:22.737
I knew it was a mistake.
I said "shut up!"

00:18:30.554 --> 00:18:32.467
Dude, I full-On swayzed that mother.

00:18:45.072 --> 00:18:46.567
What is it?

00:18:46.572 --> 00:18:48.036
Something's going on out there.

00:18:52.072 --> 00:18:53.958
All clear? Clear.

00:18:55.322 --> 00:18:57.027
Still no pulse. No.

00:18:57.471 --> 00:18:58.936
Still no pulse.

00:18:58.943 --> 00:19:01.538
Okay, let's go again. 360. Charging.

00:19:01.554 --> 00:19:03.809
All clear? Clear.

00:19:04.261 --> 00:19:07.028
Come on, come on... Still no pulse.

00:19:09.063 --> 00:19:10.038
Clear.

00:19:12.723 --> 00:19:15.337
Still nothing. Okay, let's go again.

00:19:16.452 --> 00:19:17.737
Charging.

00:19:17.742 --> 00:19:18.576
All clear?

00:19:18.583 --> 00:19:21.116
Get the hell away from me. Stay back!

00:19:23.565 --> 00:19:25.726
There's no change. Starting cpr.

00:19:25.735 --> 00:19:27.028
I said get back!

00:19:33.353 --> 00:19:34.720
Still nothing.

00:19:42.784 --> 00:19:43.668
We have a pulse.

00:19:43.994 --> 00:19:45.518
We're back into sinus rhythm.

00:20:03.333 --> 00:20:04.487
Don't worry, Sammy.

00:20:04.994 --> 00:20:06.416
I'm not going anywhere.

00:20:07.112 --> 00:20:08.840
I'm getting that thing
before it gets me.

00:20:11.982 --> 00:20:13.246
It's some kind of spirit,

00:20:14.003 --> 00:20:15.188
But I could grab it.

00:20:15.894 --> 00:20:16.989
And if I can grab it,

00:20:17.683 --> 00:20:18.639
I can kill it.

00:20:36.003 --> 00:20:37.470
Can't you see me?!

00:20:38.802 --> 00:20:40.679
Why won't you look at me?!

00:20:42.034 --> 00:20:43.208
Now what?

00:20:46.605 --> 00:20:48.588
Somebody talk to me!

00:20:48.592 --> 00:20:51.728
Say something, please! Can you see me?

00:20:52.652 --> 00:20:53.586
Yeah.

00:20:56.704 --> 00:20:58.788
All right, just calm down.

00:20:59.295 --> 00:21:00.420
What's your name?

00:21:00.424 --> 00:21:01.470
Tessa.

00:21:01.632 --> 00:21:03.288
Okay, good, Tessa. I'm Dean.

00:21:03.804 --> 00:21:05.606
What's happening to me?

00:21:06.525 --> 00:21:07.500
Am I...

00:21:07.773 --> 00:21:09.106
Am I dead?

00:21:09.114 --> 00:21:10.626
That sort of depends.

00:21:21.534 --> 00:21:23.056
I don't understand.

00:21:23.434 --> 00:21:25.599
I just came in for an appendectomy.

00:21:27.753 --> 00:21:29.739
I hate to bear bad news, but...

00:21:30.594 --> 00:21:32.489
I think there were some complications.

00:21:35.025 --> 00:21:37.329
It's just a dream, that's all.

00:21:37.333 --> 00:21:38.836
This is just

00:21:38.842 --> 00:21:40.548
A very weird,

00:21:40.722 --> 00:21:42.786
Unbelievably vivid dream.

00:21:42.793 --> 00:21:43.887
Tessa,

00:21:44.335 --> 00:21:45.639
It's not a dream.

00:21:45.893 --> 00:21:47.447
Then what else could it be?

00:21:49.733 --> 00:21:51.840
You ever heard of an
out-Of-Body experience?

00:21:52.884 --> 00:21:54.958
What are you, some new-Agey guy?

00:21:54.961 --> 00:21:57.688
You see me messing with
crystals or listening to Yanni?

00:21:59.563 --> 00:22:01.389
It's actually a very old idea.

00:22:01.963 --> 00:22:03.628
It's got a lot of different names.

00:22:03.844 --> 00:22:05.099
Bilocation,

00:22:05.603 --> 00:22:07.759
Crisis apparitions, fetches.

00:22:07.963 --> 00:22:09.666
I think it's happening to us.

00:22:09.983 --> 00:22:11.278
If it is...

00:22:12.735 --> 00:22:14.467
It  means that we're spirits...

00:22:15.235 --> 00:22:17.148
Of people close to death.

00:22:19.833 --> 00:22:21.369
So we're gonna die?

00:22:21.503 --> 00:22:22.398
No.

00:22:23.134 --> 00:22:24.208
Not if we hold on.

00:22:24.643 --> 00:22:27.467
Our bodies can get better. You can
snap right back in there and wake up.

00:22:31.353 --> 00:22:32.989
What do you mean you felt something?

00:22:32.992 --> 00:22:34.628
I mean, it felt like...

00:22:35.382 --> 00:22:36.507
Like Dean.

00:22:37.235 --> 00:22:39.539
Like he was there, just
out of eyeshot or something.

00:22:40.134 --> 00:22:42.079
I don't know if it's my
psychic thing or what.

00:22:42.351 --> 00:22:43.817
But do you think it's even possible?

00:22:43.824 --> 00:22:46.277
Do you think his spirit could be around?

00:22:46.603 --> 00:22:48.538
Anything's possible.

00:22:48.853 --> 00:22:50.528
Well, there's one way to find out.

00:22:51.204 --> 00:22:53.809
Where are you going? I got to

00:22:53.811 --> 00:22:56.606
Pick something up.
I'll be back. Wait, Sam.

00:22:56.612 --> 00:22:58.009
I promise

00:22:58.154 --> 00:22:59.878
I won't hunt this demon.

00:23:00.443 --> 00:23:02.489
Not until we know Dean's okay.

00:23:07.833 --> 00:23:09.440
I got to say, I'm impressed.

00:23:09.692 --> 00:23:11.228
With what? You.

00:23:11.603 --> 00:23:13.989
Most people in your spot
would be jello by now, but

00:23:13.992 --> 00:23:15.730
You're taking this pretty well.

00:23:15.735 --> 00:23:17.356
Maybe a little better than me.

00:23:17.634 --> 00:23:18.827
Don't get me wrong,

00:23:19.161 --> 00:23:21.288
I was pretty freaked at first. But

00:23:21.684 --> 00:23:23.849
Now I don't know. Maybe I'm dealing.

00:23:23.855 --> 00:23:25.398
So you're okay with dying?

00:23:25.403 --> 00:23:27.539
No, of course not.

00:23:28.333 --> 00:23:31.489
I  just think whatever's
gonna happen is gonna happen.

00:23:31.721 --> 00:23:33.898
It's out of my control. It's just...

00:23:33.902 --> 00:23:35.177
Fate.

00:23:37.862 --> 00:23:39.208
That's crap.

00:23:40.893 --> 00:23:42.556
You always have a choice.

00:23:43.085 --> 00:23:45.967
You can either roll over and die, you
can keep fighting no matter what...

00:23:45.983 --> 00:23:48.139
<i>Room 237. Code blue. Dr. Christie</i>

00:23:48.143 --> 00:23:50.159
Dean, where are you
going? Just wait here.

00:23:57.903 --> 00:23:59.860
Give me another amp oepi, please.

00:24:08.532 --> 00:24:10.056
Get away from her!

00:24:10.554 --> 00:24:11.516
Still nothing.

00:24:18.432 --> 00:24:20.226
All right. Let's call it.

00:24:20.963 --> 00:24:22.106
Time of death...

00:24:22.273 --> 00:24:24.018
5:11 p.M.

00:24:25.532 --> 00:24:27.467
At least she's not suffering anymore.

00:24:42.992 --> 00:24:43.809
Hey.

00:24:45.514 --> 00:24:48.186
I think maybe you're
around. And if you are,

00:24:49.425 --> 00:24:50.938
Don't make fun of me for this,

00:24:50.945 --> 00:24:51.989
But, um...

00:24:53.862 --> 00:24:55.226
But there's one way we can talk.

00:25:01.154 --> 00:25:02.717
Oh, you got to be kidding me.

00:25:18.784 --> 00:25:19.717
Dean?

00:25:24.911 --> 00:25:26.677
Dean, are you here?

00:25:31.494 --> 00:25:34.057
God, I feel like I'm at a slumber party.

00:25:36.623 --> 00:25:38.166
All right, Sam.

00:25:39.552 --> 00:25:41.318
This isn't gonna work.

00:25:59.215 --> 00:26:00.509
I'll be damned.

00:26:02.065 --> 00:26:04.059
Oh, it's good to hear from you, man.

00:26:05.054 --> 00:26:07.099
It hasn't been the
same without you, Dean.

00:26:07.103 --> 00:26:08.407
Damn straight.

00:26:10.543 --> 00:26:11.708
All right.

00:26:15.242 --> 00:26:16.217
Dean, what?

00:26:18.813 --> 00:26:19.750
" H"...

00:26:21.324 --> 00:26:22.090
"U"...

00:26:28.643 --> 00:26:29.826
"Hunt"?

00:26:30.123 --> 00:26:31.557
What, "hunting"?

00:26:31.563 --> 00:26:33.059
Are you hunting?

00:26:36.684 --> 00:26:40.067
Dean, it's in the hospital,
what you're hunting?

00:26:40.072 --> 00:26:41.869
Do you know what it is?

00:26:43.101 --> 00:26:45.007
One question at a time, dude.

00:26:46.074 --> 00:26:47.338
What is it?

00:26:51.731 --> 00:26:53.768
I don't think it's killing people.

00:26:54.311 --> 00:26:55.769
I think it's taking them...

00:26:57.012 --> 00:26:58.318
You know, when...

00:26:59.414 --> 00:27:00.878
When their time is just up.

00:27:03.612 --> 00:27:05.007
A reaper...

00:27:07.632 --> 00:27:09.119
Is it after you?

00:27:19.592 --> 00:27:21.148
If it's here naturally,

00:27:22.583 --> 00:27:24.168
There's no way to stop it.

00:27:25.143 --> 00:27:26.646
Yeah, you can't kill death.

00:27:27.425 --> 00:27:29.197
Man, you're, uh...

00:27:29.204 --> 00:27:30.326
I'm screwed, Sam.

00:27:34.902 --> 00:27:36.606
No. No, no, no.

00:27:37.554 --> 00:27:39.016
There's got to be a way.

00:27:39.483 --> 00:27:40.876
There's got to be a way.

00:27:41.641 --> 00:27:43.157
Dad will know what to do.

00:27:52.961 --> 00:27:53.779
Dad?

00:28:46.583 --> 00:28:48.987
Hey, so dad wasn't in his room.

00:28:49.134 --> 00:28:50.317
Where is he?

00:28:50.324 --> 00:28:53.057
But I got dad's journal, so...

00:28:53.342 --> 00:28:55.480
Who knows? Maybe there's
something in here.

00:29:04.822 --> 00:29:06.860
Thanks for not giving up on me, Sammy.

00:29:25.023 --> 00:29:26.849
Son of a bitch.

00:29:34.744 --> 00:29:36.248
Hi, Dean.

00:29:37.014 --> 00:29:39.570
You know, you read the
most interesting things.

00:29:40.391 --> 00:29:42.860
For example, did you know that reapers

00:29:42.864 --> 00:29:44.846
Can alter human perception?

00:29:46.762 --> 00:29:47.929
I sure didn't.

00:29:49.922 --> 00:29:53.019
Basically they can make themselves
appear however they want...

00:29:54.094 --> 00:29:55.317
Like, say...

00:29:55.884 --> 00:29:57.259
A pretty girl.

00:29:59.085 --> 00:30:01.340
You're much prettier than
the last reaper I met.

00:30:01.445 --> 00:30:03.708
I was wondering when
you'd figure it out.

00:30:05.054 --> 00:30:06.509
I should have known.

00:30:07.605 --> 00:30:12.358
That whole "accepting fate" rap of yours
is far too laid-Back for a dead chick.

00:30:12.364 --> 00:30:15.878
But, you know, the mother and the body...
I'm still trying to figure that one out.

00:30:16.262 --> 00:30:18.208
It's my sandbox.

00:30:18.463 --> 00:30:20.266
I can make you see whatever I want.

00:30:20.275 --> 00:30:22.346
What is this, like a
turn-On for you, huh?

00:30:22.532 --> 00:30:25.367
Toying with me? You
didn't give me much choice.

00:30:25.375 --> 00:30:27.820
You saw my true form,
and you flipped out.

00:30:28.804 --> 00:30:30.748
Kind of hurts a girl's feelings.

00:30:32.534 --> 00:30:35.556
This was the only way I
could get you to talk to me.

00:30:35.715 --> 00:30:36.737
Okay, fine.

00:30:37.422 --> 00:30:38.360
We're talking.

00:30:39.121 --> 00:30:40.817
What the hell do you want to talk about?

00:30:42.603 --> 00:30:44.456
How death is nothing to fear.

00:30:45.702 --> 00:30:47.418
It's your time to go, Dean.

00:30:49.125 --> 00:30:51.576
And you're living on
borrowed time already.

00:31:50.052 --> 00:31:51.699
What the hell are you
doing down here, buddy?

00:31:51.701 --> 00:31:53.159
I can explain. Yeah?

00:31:53.163 --> 00:31:56.489
You're gonna explain to
security. Come on. You follow me.

00:31:57.623 --> 00:31:58.639
Hey.

00:32:00.492 --> 00:32:02.177
How stupid you think I am?

00:32:05.134 --> 00:32:07.818
You really want an
honest answer to that?

00:32:19.034 --> 00:32:22.489
You conjuring me, John? I'm surprised.

00:32:22.494 --> 00:32:24.597
I took you for a lot of things,

00:32:24.603 --> 00:32:28.659
But suicidally reckless
wasn't one of them.

00:32:29.405 --> 00:32:31.130
I can always shoot you.

00:32:31.605 --> 00:32:33.329
You could always miss.

00:32:34.625 --> 00:32:37.246
And you only got one try, don't you?

00:32:40.184 --> 00:32:41.219
Did you

00:32:41.864 --> 00:32:43.728
Really think you could trap me?

00:32:44.931 --> 00:32:46.449
Oh, I don't want to trap you.

00:32:51.293 --> 00:32:52.677
I want to make a deal.

00:32:59.751 --> 00:33:00.860
Dean, are you here?

00:33:05.561 --> 00:33:07.327
Couldn't find anything in the book.

00:33:10.034 --> 00:33:11.646
I don't know how to help you.

00:33:14.894 --> 00:33:16.737
But I'll keep trying, all right?

00:33:17.494 --> 00:33:19.289
As long as you keep fighting.

00:33:22.875 --> 00:33:24.320
I mean, come on, you can't...

00:33:25.041 --> 00:33:28.338
You can't leave me here alone with dad.
We'll kill each other. You know that.

00:33:37.014 --> 00:33:38.806
Dean, you got to hold on.

00:33:41.454 --> 00:33:43.567
You can't go, man, not now.

00:33:46.181 --> 00:33:48.317
We were just starting
to be brothers again.

00:33:52.373 --> 00:33:53.797
Can you hear me?

00:33:55.985 --> 00:33:57.896
Look, I'm sure you've
heard this before, but...

00:33:59.391 --> 00:34:02.327
You got to make an exception.
You got to cut me a break.

00:34:03.061 --> 00:34:04.628
Stage 3...

00:34:04.632 --> 00:34:05.846
Bargaining.

00:34:08.552 --> 00:34:10.009
I'm serious.

00:34:11.644 --> 00:34:13.568
My family is in danger.

00:34:14.545 --> 00:34:16.467
See, we're kind of in
the middle of this, uh...

00:34:17.045 --> 00:34:18.717
War.

00:34:19.083 --> 00:34:21.826
And they need me. The fight's over.

00:34:21.831 --> 00:34:24.496
No, it isn't. It is for you.

00:34:25.181 --> 00:34:26.789
Dean...

00:34:26.932 --> 00:34:29.938
You're not the first soldier
I've plucked from the field.

00:34:30.621 --> 00:34:32.048
They all feel the same.

00:34:32.684 --> 00:34:34.496
They can't leave.

00:34:34.704 --> 00:34:37.239
Victory hangs in the balance.

00:34:37.284 --> 00:34:38.567
But they're wrong.

00:34:39.514 --> 00:34:42.340
The battle goes on
without them. My brother,

00:34:42.344 --> 00:34:43.748
He could die without me.

00:34:44.012 --> 00:34:45.489
Maybe he will.

00:34:46.224 --> 00:34:47.739
Maybe he won't.

00:34:48.603 --> 00:34:50.797
Nothing you can do about it.

00:34:56.523 --> 00:34:58.480
It's an honorable death,

00:34:59.041 --> 00:35:00.809
A warrior's death.

00:35:01.853 --> 00:35:04.429
I think I'll pass on
the 72 virgins, thanks.

00:35:05.201 --> 00:35:07.338
I'm not that into prude chicks anyway.

00:35:07.342 --> 00:35:08.909
That's funny.

00:35:09.023 --> 00:35:10.447
You're very cute.

00:35:12.371 --> 00:35:14.628
There's no such thing
as an honorable death.

00:35:15.634 --> 00:35:19.059
My corpse is gonna rot in the
ground, and my family is gonna die.

00:35:22.061 --> 00:35:23.347
No.

00:35:25.994 --> 00:35:28.358
I'm not going with you.
I don't care what you do.

00:35:31.313 --> 00:35:32.257
Well,

00:35:32.603 --> 00:35:34.096
Like you said...

00:35:35.152 --> 00:35:36.807
There's always a choice.

00:35:37.242 --> 00:35:39.396
I can't make you come with me.

00:35:39.925 --> 00:35:41.130
But,

00:35:41.795 --> 00:35:43.849
You're not getting back in your body.

00:35:44.594 --> 00:35:46.208
And that's just facts.

00:35:47.182 --> 00:35:48.467
So, yes,

00:35:48.474 --> 00:35:49.746
You can stay.

00:35:49.862 --> 00:35:51.797
You'll stay here for years...

00:35:52.342 --> 00:35:53.679
Disembodied.

00:35:53.831 --> 00:35:55.110
Scared.

00:35:55.221 --> 00:35:58.099
And over the decades, it'll
probably drive you mad.

00:35:58.983 --> 00:36:01.148
Maybe you'll even get violent.

00:36:01.304 --> 00:36:02.980
What are you saying?

00:36:06.052 --> 00:36:08.469
How do you think angry spirits are born?

00:36:09.862 --> 00:36:11.400
They can't let go,

00:36:11.413 --> 00:36:13.159
And they can't move on.

00:36:13.443 --> 00:36:15.489
And you're about to become one.

00:36:16.353 --> 00:36:18.367
The same thing you hunt.

00:36:21.934 --> 00:36:24.077
It's very unsinly,

00:36:24.083 --> 00:36:25.829
Making deals with devils.

00:36:27.764 --> 00:36:30.559
How do I know this
isn't just another trick?

00:36:30.672 --> 00:36:32.288
It's no trick.

00:36:33.463 --> 00:36:35.226
I will give you the colt

00:36:35.623 --> 00:36:37.027
And the bullet.

00:36:37.704 --> 00:36:39.757
But you got to help Dean.

00:36:41.614 --> 00:36:43.519
You got to bring him back.

00:36:44.384 --> 00:36:47.150
Why, John, you're a sentimentalist.

00:36:49.014 --> 00:36:50.420
If only your boys

00:36:50.862 --> 00:36:52.757
Knew how much their daddy loved them.

00:36:53.461 --> 00:36:54.900
It's a good trade.

00:36:56.233 --> 00:36:59.759
You care hell of a lot more
about this gun than you do Dean.

00:36:59.762 --> 00:37:01.009
Don't be so sure.

00:37:01.621 --> 00:37:04.179
He killed some people
very special to me.

00:37:06.362 --> 00:37:08.697
But, still, you're right.
He isn't much of a threat.

00:37:08.704 --> 00:37:11.748
And neither is your other son,

00:37:11.862 --> 00:37:12.967
Of course.

00:37:16.682 --> 00:37:18.157
You know the truth,

00:37:18.161 --> 00:37:19.210
Right?

00:37:20.724 --> 00:37:22.219
About Sammy...

00:37:22.815 --> 00:37:24.246
And the other children?

00:37:24.713 --> 00:37:25.586
Yeah.

00:37:26.103 --> 00:37:27.786
I've known for a while.

00:37:27.795 --> 00:37:31.559
But Sam doesn't, does he?
You've been playing dumb.

00:37:32.112 --> 00:37:34.059
Can you bring Dean back?

00:37:34.652 --> 00:37:36.719
Yes or no.

00:37:36.722 --> 00:37:37.927
No.

00:37:38.945 --> 00:37:40.737
But I know someone who can.

00:37:41.855 --> 00:37:43.186
It's not a problem.

00:37:44.065 --> 00:37:44.949
Good.

00:37:45.664 --> 00:37:47.666
And before I give you the gun,

00:37:48.244 --> 00:37:50.630
I'm gonna want to make
sure that Dean's okay,

00:37:50.643 --> 00:37:52.269
With my own eyes.

00:37:52.271 --> 00:37:54.159
Oh, John, I'm offended.

00:37:54.163 --> 00:37:55.686
Don't you trust me?

00:38:00.483 --> 00:38:01.427
Fine.

00:38:03.001 --> 00:38:06.427
So we have a deal? No, John, not yet.

00:38:06.434 --> 00:38:09.019
You still need to sweeten the pot.

00:38:09.452 --> 00:38:10.778
With what?

00:38:12.793 --> 00:38:16.009
There's something else I want

00:38:16.333 --> 00:38:17.800
As much as that gun.

00:38:19.282 --> 00:38:20.606
Maybe more.

00:38:22.893 --> 00:38:24.838
It's time to put the pain behind you.

00:38:28.031 --> 00:38:29.356
And go where?

00:38:30.751 --> 00:38:31.807
Sorry.

00:38:32.684 --> 00:38:35.027
I can't give away the big punch line.

00:38:41.061 --> 00:38:42.388
Moment of truth.

00:38:44.321 --> 00:38:46.099
No changing your mind later.

00:38:49.223 --> 00:38:50.869
So, what's it going to be?

00:39:11.875 --> 00:39:13.288
What are you doing that for?

00:39:14.302 --> 00:39:15.408
I'm not doing it.

00:39:17.213 --> 00:39:18.667
What the hell...!

00:39:18.674 --> 00:39:20.197
You can't do this!

00:39:20.375 --> 00:39:21.838
Get away!

00:39:22.224 --> 00:39:23.817
What's happening?!

00:39:34.163 --> 00:39:36.076
Today's your lucky day, kid.

00:39:39.873 --> 00:39:40.908
Dean!

00:39:41.991 --> 00:39:43.869
Help! I need help!

00:39:45.644 --> 00:39:46.766
I can't explain it.

00:39:46.951 --> 00:39:48.266
The edema has vanished.

00:39:48.433 --> 00:39:50.418
The internal contusions are healed.

00:39:50.804 --> 00:39:52.067
Your vitals are good.

00:39:53.152 --> 00:39:55.307
You got to have some kind
of angel watching over you.

00:39:55.893 --> 00:39:57.077
Thanks, doc.

00:40:01.481 --> 00:40:03.056
You said a reaper was after me?

00:40:03.062 --> 00:40:03.927
Yeah.

00:40:04.272 --> 00:40:05.366
How did I ditch it?

00:40:05.542 --> 00:40:06.636
You got me.

00:40:07.934 --> 00:40:09.549
Dean, you really don't
remember anything?

00:40:09.994 --> 00:40:10.877
No.

00:40:11.625 --> 00:40:12.730
Except this

00:40:13.043 --> 00:40:14.518
Pit in my stomach.

00:40:15.822 --> 00:40:17.406
Sam, something's wrong.

00:40:20.932 --> 00:40:22.386
How you feeling, dude?

00:40:23.022 --> 00:40:24.248
Fine, I guess.

00:40:25.181 --> 00:40:26.259
I'm alive.

00:40:26.384 --> 00:40:28.117
That's what matters.

00:40:28.521 --> 00:40:29.818
Where were you last night?

00:40:32.583 --> 00:40:34.288
I had some things to take care of.

00:40:34.754 --> 00:40:36.257
Well, that's specific.

00:40:36.942 --> 00:40:38.417
Come on, Sam.

00:40:39.184 --> 00:40:40.817
Did you go after the demon?

00:40:42.773 --> 00:40:43.726
No.

00:40:43.733 --> 00:40:46.328
You know, why don't I
believe you right now?

00:40:52.804 --> 00:40:54.447
Can we not fight?

00:40:56.094 --> 00:40:59.329
You know, half the time we're fighting,
I don't know what we're fighting about.

00:40:59.335 --> 00:41:00.647
We're just butting heads.

00:41:02.134 --> 00:41:04.099
Look, Sammy, I've...

00:41:04.534 --> 00:41:06.367
I've made some mistakes.

00:41:07.894 --> 00:41:10.608
But I've always done the best I could.

00:41:12.422 --> 00:41:14.478
I just don't want to
fight anymore, okay?

00:41:16.422 --> 00:41:18.147
Dad, are you all right?

00:41:21.041 --> 00:41:22.196
Yeah.

00:41:22.684 --> 00:41:24.469
Yeah, I'm just a little tired.

00:41:25.961 --> 00:41:27.777
Hey, son, would you mind, uh...

00:41:28.693 --> 00:41:30.998
Would you mind getting
me a cup of caffeine?

00:41:31.051 --> 00:41:33.219
Yeah. Yeah, sure.

00:41:54.714 --> 00:41:56.179
What is it?

00:41:58.201 --> 00:41:59.509
You know, when, uh...

00:42:00.283 --> 00:42:01.898
When you were a kid,

00:42:03.974 --> 00:42:05.739
I'd come home from a hunt,

00:42:07.132 --> 00:42:09.978
And after what I'd seen, I'd be...

00:42:11.031 --> 00:42:12.607
I'd be wrecked.

00:42:13.454 --> 00:42:15.109
And you...

00:42:16.134 --> 00:42:17.956
You'd come up to me, and

00:42:17.961 --> 00:42:21.116
You'd put your hand on my shoulder, and
you'd look me in the eye, and you'd...

00:42:26.463 --> 00:42:28.427
You'd say, "it's okay, dad".

00:42:36.302 --> 00:42:38.127
I'm sorry.

00:42:39.792 --> 00:42:41.597
Why?

00:42:43.932 --> 00:42:47.730
You shouldn't have had to say that to
me. I should've been saying that to you.

00:42:49.442 --> 00:42:51.098
You know, I put...

00:42:52.331 --> 00:42:56.177
I put too much on your shoulders.
I made you grow up too fast.

00:42:57.873 --> 00:43:00.516
You took care of Sammy.
You took care of me.

00:43:02.163 --> 00:43:03.967
You did that.

00:43:04.681 --> 00:43:06.658
And you didn't complain. Not once.

00:43:11.652 --> 00:43:13.980
I just want you to know...

00:43:15.152 --> 00:43:17.597
That I am so proud of you.

00:43:20.764 --> 00:43:22.687
Is it really you talking?

00:43:22.692 --> 00:43:23.597
Yeah.

00:43:24.011 --> 00:43:25.686
Yeah, it's really me.

00:43:27.594 --> 00:43:29.607
Why are you saying this stuff?

00:43:37.882 --> 00:43:40.768
I want you to watch out for Sammy, okay?

00:43:41.704 --> 00:43:43.548
Yeah, dad, you know I will.

00:43:44.714 --> 00:43:46.106
You're scaring me.

00:43:47.894 --> 00:43:49.866
Don't be scared, Dean.

00:44:47.362 --> 00:44:48.429
Okay.

00:45:01.532 --> 00:45:02.528
Dad?

00:45:23.223 --> 00:45:25.308
No, no, no, it's our dad. It's our dad!

00:45:27.491 --> 00:45:29.748
Okay. Let's try again.
An amp of atropine.

00:45:29.751 --> 00:45:30.627
Come on...

00:45:37.101 --> 00:45:38.697
Okay. Stop compression.

00:45:46.232 --> 00:45:48.239
Come on, come on. Still no pulse.

00:45:49.594 --> 00:45:51.998
Okay. That's it,
everybody. I'll call it.

00:45:53.443 --> 00:45:56.139
Time of death, 10:41 a.M.



00:04:34.476 --> 00:04:35.976
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
